  "interpretation": "Joint SSVS (So, Chen, Liu 2006) simultaneously searches mean and variance equation variable subsets via joint MCMC. This addresses the concern that sequential selection (K433 mean-only, then K484/K821 variance-only) might miss cross-equation interactions where a variable becomes important in one equation conditional on another variable being in the other equation. The joint posterior sampling can detect such synergies. The finding that even joint selection yields NULL for external variables strongly confirms the self-sufficiency of GJR internal dynamics for SPY volatility prediction.",
